ATTACK 1 — REAL DATA (default full-history window + 2025-04 window)
  Harness: probe_cb4_test.go added only to the two throwaway copies,
  calling Initialize()+LoadDataContext() against the copied real CSVs,
  then buildMajorExpenseChartData / bucketMajorExpenses / an httptest
  call into handleMajorExpenseDrilldown, identically in both trees.
  - Full-history window: bucketMajorExpenses reports
    Travel & vacations total=-159.950000 (25 txns). buildMajorExpenseChartData's
    "credits" list carries {"name":"Travel & vacations","amount":-159.95000000000005}.
    handleMajorExpenseDrilldown(name=Travel & vacations, full window) returns
    {"Total":-159.95,"Count":25} — same signed net (floating accumulation of
    the same 25 txns; -159.95 vs -159.95000000000005 is the same number to
    the cent, not a divergent figure). PASS on cross-surface consistency.
  - Positive wedge set, full window: python3-loaded JSON, `labels` list
    and `values` list from fixed vs master compared with `==` (exact
    Python list/float equality, no rtk in the path) -> IDENTICAL on both
    labels and values (8 named wedges + "Other"=45187.21). `smaller` list
    also byte-for-byte identical. Master has no "credits" key (expected —
    the field didn't exist pre-fix).
  - 2025-04 window: no transaction in that calendar month matches
    "Travel & vacations" (0 txns; the refund-heavy cruise entries are
    dated 2025-03-30, outside 04-01..04-30), so credits is absent for that
    window in both trees — not a failure, just an empty case; wedge sets
    for that window are also byte-identical fixed vs master.
  No wedge gained, lost, or changed value on either window. MET.

